---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service, SyncSet"
  description="The terms that apply when you engage SyncSet to audit, design or build workflow automation for your business."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="legal">
      <div class="legal__container">
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: 14 September 2026</p>

        <p>
          These terms govern your use of syncset.com.au and the workflow-audit and automation-build services SyncSet provides.
        </p>

        <h2>The free Diagnostic</h2>
        <p>
          The free Automation Diagnostic is free and creates no obligation on either side. You answer a short set of questions about how enquiries move through your business, and we send you a report on what it's costing you and what we'd build. No work starts and no payment is requested from a free Diagnostic alone.
        </p>

        <h2>Paid work</h2>
        <p>
          Any paid engagement, a pilot or a full build, is governed by a separate written scope of work that we send you before any payment or work begins. That document sets out price, deliverables, and timeline, and takes precedence over these general terms for that engagement.
        </p>
        <p>
          Prices on this site are in Australian dollars and include GST. SyncSet is registered for GST (ABN 72 436 500 217) and issues a tax invoice for every paid engagement. For clients outside Australia, GST treatment is set out in the scope of work.
        </p>

        <h2>What we don't do</h2>
        <p>
          SyncSet builds and maintains workflow automations. We don't provide legal, financial, tax, or medical advice, and nothing on this site should be read as such. Automation workflows are built to the specification you approve; you review and sign off before anything goes live.
        </p>

        <h2>Ownership</h2>
        <p>
          You own everything we build for you, the workflows, the integrations, the data that flows through them, from the day it's delivered. If you stop working with us, the system keeps running in your accounts; we don't hold anything back.
        </p>

        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable care to build reliable automations and to fix anything that breaks that we built. We're not liable for failures in third-party tools we connect to (your CRM, calendar, messaging platform, and similar) that are outside our control, or for losses arising from how you use the systems we build. Nothing in these terms limits any consumer guarantee you're entitled to under the Australian Consumer Law that can't lawfully be excluded.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms as our services change. Continued use of the site after an update means you accept the current version.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of New South Wales, Australia.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
<a href="mailto:contact@syncset.com.au">contact@syncset.com.au</a>

        <p class="legal__disclaimer">
          <strong>⚠️ Note:</strong> This draft was prepared by Claude, not a lawyer; it is not legal advice. Before publishing, confirm: whether the liability wording actually protects you given SyncSet's entity structure (sole trader vs. registered company changes your personal exposure, and may warrant an explicit liability cap backed by insurance); whether a separate signed scope-of-work per client is your actual current practice or still aspirational; and whether the Australian Consumer Law guarantee wording matches current ACCC guidance for a services business.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    min-height: calc(100vh - 200px);
    padding: var(--space-24) var(--gutter);
    background-color: var(--paper);
  }

  .legal__container {
    max-width: var(--max-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: var(--graphite);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .legal__container h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .legal__updated {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--graphite);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  .legal__container h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .legal__container p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .legal__container strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .legal__container a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal__disclaimer {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .legal {
      padding: var(--space-16) var(--gutter);
    }

    .legal__container h1 {
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
